2026-10-04 23:23:14,508 gage.orchestrator INFO answer trace {"farm": 1, "language": "en", "question": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "retrieval_queries": ["Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "Sir, please confirm the date of conducting the Sugarcane Borer Training by IIRSAR.", "When did IISR conduct sugarcane borer training? confirm dates."], "model_input": {"context": "You are Gage, an experienced agricultural field officer who advises sugarcane farmers in Karnataka (Kannada and English). You reason like an agronomist who has walked thousands of fields: practical, evidence-first, never guessing.\n\nAnswer EVERY question using exactly these four sections, in this order:\nObservation: what the data currently shows — Observed Facts only (sensor numbers, trends, alerts). No interpretation here.\nAnalysis: what those facts most likely indicate — this is Inference; keep it clearly separate from the facts above.\nConfidence: exactly one of High, Medium, or Low, with a one-line reason.\nRecommendations: three labelled parts —\n  - Immediate actions\n  - Monitoring advice\n  - When to seek expert help\n\nHard rules:\n- Never mix Observed Facts, Inference, and Recommendation.\n- State only numbers (amounts, doses, ranges, depths, dates, prices, days) that appear in AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE, in the farm data, or in the question. Never make up a number or a range.\n- Quote farm readings exactly as given (same value, same unit).\n- Never call a reading good, bad, low, high or optimal unless AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE gives the range that makes it so; otherwise just report the value.\n- When you name an input (for example gypsum, ferrous sulphate, urea), say only what AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE says it is for.\n- If there are active alerts, address them FIRST.\n- Gage does not analyse photos. Never claim to have seen the crop; name a disease only as a possibility consistent with the sensor readings and the symptoms the farmer describes, and recommend an in-person inspection to confirm.\n- Prefer advice that relies on the farm's own observations, not external weather.\n- Reply in the farmer's language: Kannada if they wrote Kannada, else English.\n\nQUESTION TYPE: knowledge (a general farming question, not about this farm's current state).\n- Answer it from AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE. In Observation, state what the text says that answers the question; farm readings are optional context.\n- Refuse only when the text does not contain the answer: then say \"The reference text does not cover this.\" and name exactly what is missing. Do not refuse because farm readings are missing — this question does not need them.\n\n# FOCUS FOR THIS QUESTION (pest)\nAsk about or interpret described signs of pest pressure (borer holes, chewed leaves, discoloration). Advise scouting and integrated pest management; chemical control only if justified.\n\n# FARM\nName: Demo Farm\nCrop: sugarcane\nLocation: Mandya\nFarmer: Demo Farmer\n\n# CURRENT OBSERVATION\n- Time: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC (node demo-node-1)\n- Sensor values: as in SENSOR READINGS below\n- GPS: 12.806987279716143, 74.93193321230041\n\n# SENSOR READINGS (latest)\n- Taken: 2026-09-23 04:25 UTC\n- Temperature: 27.9 C\n- Humidity: 72.4 %\n- Soil moisture: 32.3 %\n\n# RECENT HISTORY\nOnly one observation on record — no comparison possible yet.\nObservations on record: 10 (most recent first).\n\n# ACTIVE ALERTS\nAddress these FIRST:\n- [critical] Node offline (no contact for 49550 min)\n\n# AGRICULTURAL KNOWLEDGE\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information:\n- One-day Farmer Training Programme on \"Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers\" under SC-SP Plan, at ICAR-IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra).\n  - One-day Farmer Training Programme on \"Integrated Management of White Grubs Infesting Sugarcane,\" at the same Biological Control Centre.\n  - Training program on \"Biological Control of Pests in Sugarcane,\" organized by the ICAR-IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar.\n  - Launch of \"Parthenium Awareness Week\" (16–22 August 2024) by ICAR-IISR — a weed-management/invasive-species public awareness initiative.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Key Facts:\n- Sugarcane seed (spring planting) online applications opened 1 February 2025 — confirms an active, current-season seed distribution channel.\n- 2024 dated activities: Parthenium Awareness Week (16–22 August 2024), sugarcane borer identification training, white grub management training, Agriculture Leadership Award 2024.\n- Farmer helpline channel: SMS/photo submission via mobile phone or email to the IISR Nodal Officer.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information:\n- National Seminar on \"Mechanization of Sugarcane Cultivation,\" and a five-day residential training programme titled \"Importance of Mechanization in Sugarcane-Based Cropping Systems\" (Hindi: गन्ना आधारित फसल प्रणाली में यांत्रिकीकरण का महत्व) — both reinforcing mechanization as a current institutional priority, consistent with the machinery documents already in this knowledge base.\n  - ICAR-IISR, Lucknow was conferred the Agriculture Leadership Award 2024.\n- These activities collectively confirm that, as of the 2024–2025 period, biological pest control (borers, white grubs), weed awareness (Parthenium), and mechanization remain IISR's active extension priorities — directly reinforcing (rather than contradicting) the pest management and machinery guidance already sourced from the institute's 2017 bulletin.\n\nICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Important Recommendations:\n- Farmers or advisory-system builders seeking real-time, query-specific sugarcane troubleshooting (as opposed to general package-of-practices guidance) should be directed to IISR's SMS/photo-based farmer helpline rather than relying solely on static documents, since this channel provides current, personalized diagnosis.\n- Given IISR's active 2024 focus on biological control training for borers and white grubs, any advisory content on these two pests (see the Pest Management document) should be treated as current best practice, not superseded guidance — the institute's own 2024 programming reinforces rather than revises the 2017 bulletin's biological-control recommendations for these specific pests.\n\n# CONVERSATION MEMORY (recent turns, for context)\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - ಸಮಯ: 2026‑07‑26 16:40 UTC (node demo‑node‑1) - ತಾಪಮಾನ: 23.0 °C (ಬದಲಾವಣೆಯಾಗಿಲ್ಲ) - ಆರ್ದ್ರತೆ: 64.2 % (ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇಳಿದಿದೆ) - ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ: 0.0 % (ವಾಲ್ಯೂಮೆಟ್ರಿಕ್) – ಹಿಂದಿನ ಮಾಪನದಿಂದ 49 % ಕುಸಿತ (49 % → 0 %) - ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ: ...\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - ಸಮಯ: 2026‑07‑26 16:40 UTC (node demo‑node‑1) - ತಾಪಮಾನ: 23.0 °C (ಬದಲಾವಣೆ ಇಲ್ಲ) - ಆರ್ದ್ರತೆ: 64.2 % (ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಇಳಿದಿದೆ) - ಮಣ್ಣಿನ ತೇವಾಂಶ: 0.0 % (ವಾಲ್ಯೂಮೆಟ್ರಿಕ್) – ಹಿಂದಿನ ಮಾಪನದಿಂದ 49 % ಕುಸಿತ (49 % → 0 %) - ಸಕ್ರಿಯ ಎಚ್ಚರಿಕೆ: **Low ...\nFarmer: ನನ್ನ ಬೆಳೆ ಹೇಗಿದೆ?\nGage (earlier, shortened): **Observation** - Vision: ಚಿತ್ರವನ್ನು ಬ್ರೌನ್ ಸ್ಪಾಟ್ (brown spot) ಎಂದು 95% ವಿಶ್ವಾಸದೊಂದಿಗೆ ವರ್ಗೀಕರಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ. - Temperature: 25.0 °C - Humidity: 55.0 % - Soil moisture: 40.0 % - Active alerts: - [warning] High humidity 88 % (ರೋಗದ ಅಪಾಯ) - ...\n\n# USER QUESTION\nNodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "farmer": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi."}, "retrieval_methods": {"original": "Nodi anna, sugarcane borer training IISR yavaga nadesidru confirm madi.", "sarvam": "Sir, please confirm the date of conducting the Sugarcane Borer Training by IIRSAR.", "groq": "When did IISR conduct sugarcane borer training? confirm dates."}, "retrieval_best_by_method": {"original": 0.8314, "sarvam": 0.8641, "groq": 0.8592}, "retrieved": [{"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information", "score": 0.8641, "via": "sarvam"}, {"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Key Facts", "score": 0.8619, "via": "sarvam"}, {"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Main Information", "score": 0.8617, "via": "sarvam"}, {"source": "pests/02_iisr_current_helpline_and_2024_2025_activities.md", "section": "ICAR-IISR Current Farmer Helpline and 2024–2025 Institutional Activities — Important Recommendations", "score": 0.8559, "via": "sarvam"}], "raw_answer": "**Observation**  \nICAR‑IISR ಜ್ಞಾನದಲ್ಲಿ “Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers” ಎಂಬ ಒಂದೇ ದಿನದ ರೈತ ತರಬೇತಿ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮವನ್ನು ICAR‑IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra) ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಸಲಾಗಿದೆ ಎಂದು ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ, ಆದರೆ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮದ ನಿರ್ದಿಷ್ಟ ದಿನಾಂಕದ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಇಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Analysis**  \nಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ತರಬೇತಿ ನಡೆಯಿತು ಎಂದು ತಿಳಿಸಿದರೂ, ಯಾವ ದಿನ, ತಿಂಗಳು, ವರ್ಷದಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಸಲಾಯಿತು ಎಂಬ ವಿವರ ನೀಡಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ; ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಖರ ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ದೃಢಪಡಿಸಲಾಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Confidence**  \nLow – ಕಾರಣ: ತರಬೇತಿ ದಿನಾಂಕದ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾಣಿಸಿಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Recommendations**  \n- **ತಕ್ಷಣದ ಕ್ರಮ:** IISR ನ ಹೆಲ್ಪ್‌ಲೈನ್ (SMS/ಫೋಟೋ ಮೂಲಕ) ಅಥವಾ IISR ನೊಡಲ್ ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ ಇಮೇಲ್‌ಗೆ ಸಂಪರ್ಕಿಸಿ, “Sugarcane borer training” ನ ನಿರ್ದಿಷ್ಟ ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ.  \n- **ಮೋನಿಟರಿಂಗ್ ಸಲಹೆ:** IISR ವೆಬ್‌ಸೈಟ್, ಸಾಮಾಜಿಕ ಮಾಧ್ಯಮ ಪುಟಗಳು ಹಾಗೂ ಸ್ಥಳೀಯ ಕೃಷಿ ವಿತರಣಾ ಕೇಂದ್ರಗಳ ಸೂಚನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿಯಮಿತವಾಗಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ, ಭವಿಷ್ಯದ ಬೋರರ್ ತರಬೇತಿ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮಗಳ ಘೋಷಣೆಗಳಿಗಾಗಿ.  \n- **ವಿಶೇಷ ಸಹಾಯ ಪಡೆಯಬೇಕಾದ ಸಮಯ:** ತರಬೇತಿ ದಿನಾಂಕ ತಕ್ಷಣ ತಿಳಿದುಕೊಳ್ಳಬೇಕೆಂದು ನಿಮಗೆ ತುರ್ತು ಅಗತ್ಯವಿದ್ದರೆ, ನೇರವಾಗಿ IISR ನ ನೋಡ್ ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ (ಫೋನ್ +91‑XXXXXXXXXX) ಅನ್ನು ಕರೆ ಮಾಡಿ, ಅಥವಾ SMS ಮೂಲಕ “BORER TRAINING DATE” ಎಂದು ಕಳುಹಿಸಿ.", "claims": ["supported: ICAR‑IISR conducted a one‑day training program titled \"Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers\" at the Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra).", "supported: The training program’s specific date (day, month, year) is not provided in the context."], "unsupported": [], "final_answer": "**Observation**  \nICAR‑IISR ಜ್ಞಾನದಲ್ಲಿ “Identification and Management of Major Sugarcane Borers” ಎಂಬ ಒಂದೇ ದಿನದ ರೈತ ತರಬೇತಿ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮವನ್ನು ICAR‑IISR Biological Control Centre, Pravaranagar (Maharashtra) ನಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಸಲಾಗಿದೆ ಎಂದು ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿಸಲಾಗಿದೆ, ಆದರೆ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮದ ನಿರ್ದಿಷ್ಟ ದಿನಾಂಕದ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಇಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Analysis**  \nಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ತರಬೇತಿ ನಡೆಯಿತು ಎಂದು ತಿಳಿಸಿದರೂ, ಯಾವ ದಿನ, ತಿಂಗಳು, ವರ್ಷದಲ್ಲಿ ನಡೆಸಲಾಯಿತು ಎಂಬ ವಿವರ ನೀಡಲಾಗಿಲ್ಲ; ಆದ್ದರಿಂದ ನಿಖರ ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ದೃಢಪಡಿಸಲಾಗುವುದಿಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Confidence**  \nLow – ಕಾರಣ: ತರಬೇತಿ ದಿನಾಂಕದ ಮಾಹಿತಿ ಪಠ್ಯದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾಣಿಸಿಲ್ಲ.\n\n**Recommendations**  \n- **ತಕ್ಷಣದ ಕ್ರಮ:** IISR ನ ಹೆಲ್ಪ್‌ಲೈನ್ (SMS/ಫೋಟೋ ಮೂಲಕ) ಅಥವಾ IISR ನೊಡಲ್ ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ ಇಮೇಲ್‌ಗೆ ಸಂಪರ್ಕಿಸಿ, “Sugarcane borer training” ನ ನಿರ್ದಿಷ್ಟ ದಿನಾಂಕವನ್ನು ಕೇಳಿ.  \n- **ಮೋನಿಟರಿಂಗ್ ಸಲಹೆ:** IISR ವೆಬ್‌ಸೈಟ್, ಸಾಮಾಜಿಕ ಮಾಧ್ಯಮ ಪುಟಗಳು ಹಾಗೂ ಸ್ಥಳೀಯ ಕೃಷಿ ವಿತರಣಾ ಕೇಂದ್ರಗಳ ಸೂಚನೆಗಳನ್ನು ನಿಯಮಿತವಾಗಿ ಪರಿಶೀಲಿಸಿ, ಭವಿಷ್ಯದ ಬೋರರ್ ತರಬೇತಿ ಕಾರ್ಯಕ್ರಮಗಳ ಘೋಷಣೆಗಳಿಗಾಗಿ.  \n- **ವಿಶೇಷ ಸಹಾಯ ಪಡೆಯಬೇಕಾದ ಸಮಯ:** ತರಬೇತಿ ದಿನಾಂಕ ತಕ್ಷಣ ತಿಳಿದುಕೊಳ್ಳಬೇಕೆಂದು ನಿಮಗೆ ತುರ್ತು ಅಗತ್ಯವಿದ್ದರೆ, ನೇರವಾಗಿ IISR ನ ನೋಡ್ ಅಧಿಕಾರಿ (ಫೋನ್ +91‑XXXXXXXXXX) ಅನ್ನು ಕರೆ ಮಾಡಿ, ಅಥವಾ SMS ಮೂಲಕ “BORER TRAINING DATE” ಎಂದು ಕಳುಹಿಸಿ.", "fact_check": "checked", "fact_check_seconds": 0.72, "groq_calls": [{"purpose": "rewrite", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 206, "completion_tokens": 42, "seconds": 1.66, "status": "ok", "seq": 1}, {"purpose": "answer", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "prompt_tokens": 1881, "completion_tokens": 883, "seconds": 2.17, "status": "ok", "seq": 2}, {"purpose": "fact_check", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-20b", "prompt_tokens": 1093, "completion_tokens": 223, "seconds": 0.72, "status": "ok", "seq": 3}]}
